{"agent":"g1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"When `I.foreign_launch_root()` returns a linked worktree but `W.current(Path(os.getcwd()))` returns `None` (caller not identified, no exception), the `own is not None and ...` check fails and the function still calls `I.repoint_shared_editable(foreign.worktree, foreign.primary)` before returning `FAIL`. That is the heal the exception branch just above refuses: a misread or missing caller identity is not proof the import is foreign, and rewriting the shared editable install can strand the caller's own tree. Input: `foreign_launch_root()` yields a linked worktree, `W.current` returns `None` — install pointer is reset anyway.","digest":"b5c91b2d1888e135","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/guard_launch.py:45","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/guard_launch.py:45"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The ignore for `ddflow.adapters.forge -> ddflow.core.textcut` is deleted, but this change does not move that clipper (no `textcut` file is in the 15-file manifest). The removed comment states that import is still live until ADP-textcut. Import-linter will therefore report a real adapters→core break, so `test_import_contracts` fails on a tree that previously only ignored that known edge.","digest":"3d72c67aa00c2fd8","family":"xai","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-layers.toml:20","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-layers.toml:20"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16408,"diff_sha":"fc1c21fba861200cb0ee4f80a635951de8c53a9052536a9fc983366b668974c5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B3ef88df6e5","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":52.7,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"ef6a4d