{"agent":"g1-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"On a foreign launch whose own tree is identifiable and different, `repoint_shared_editable` is treated as success even when it did not rewrite the install. `install_info` swallows `OSError` around both `fsio.atomic_write` calls and returns normally, and this guard also does `except Exception: pass`, then always prints that the shared editable install was reset to `foreign.primary`. Given a read-only `direct_url.json` / `.pth` (or a full disk), every write fails, the process still exits `FAIL` with that “was reset — re-run” text, and the next invocation imports the same foreign worktree. The operator is told the heal happened when the checkout is unchanged.","digest":"8975357f502de87d","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/guard_launch.py:51","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/guard_launch.py:51"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16408,"diff_sha":"fc1c21fba861200cb0ee4f80a635951de8c53a9052536a9fc983366b668974c5","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B3ef88df6e5","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":121.7,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"c3b78bbfe3552dbb","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B3ef88df6e5.critic.grok-4.7.20261111T101829Z-f81a1d46.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"13463266f991ed57fb3395321ef0437d308d1731","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/guard_launch.py":"100644 19b742a60218267ef43b88e034794c4842d6e15c","ddflow/api/perf.py":"100644 36abb49b43f8d45e13247a96204aed6c68672c78","ddflow/api/perfreport.py":"100644 34b585c2d95430d857bb6a19ba33ac16fde6f77a","ddflow/api/surf_reporting.py":"100644 074d346607a74d63946c02a19430cd1ded837036","ddflow/services/bugreport.py":"100644 59651449dfe